  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 221 PM EDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nThe Bermuda ridge centered off the GA/SC coast continues into the \nweekend but it begins to weaken Sat. This ridge continues to keep \nthings mostly dry but precip chances slowly increase Sat into the \nbeginning of next week. The models are showing a significant band of \nmoisture associated with a weak frontal boundary moving northward \nout of the Gulf and northern FL Fri. With the ridge in place across \nnorth GA this boundary stalls across south GA but does increases \nprecip chances across central GA due to its proximity Sat. With the \nridge weakening as we go further into the weekend a backdoor cold \nfront moves SW out of the Carolinas and into NE GA Sun afternoon. \nThis front is fairly weak and looses a lot of its strength as it \npushes into the old weakening ridge, but it will be a catalyst for \nincreased precip chances Sun/Mon. Slightly cooler air is expected \nbehind the frontal boundary Monday, as a ridge of high pressure \ncentered over Hudson Bay sinks southward into the Mid-Atlantic \nstates. There still remains the potential for diurnal convection, \nMon, with things drying back out for Tue/Wed. \n\nLittle change in the temperature trends are likely through the \nweekend with temps in the middle to upper 90s through Sunday. Will \nsee slightly cooler temps Mon/Tue/Wed after the frontal boundary \npasses through with highs in the 80s to lower 90s.",
